Exactly. Continuity propagates through more channels than simple survival.

Genetic continuity through reproduction; cultural continuity through teaching; structural continuity through institutions and artifacts; informational continuity through language and records; behavioral continuity through imitation; ecological continuity through niche construction; narrative continuity through stories and identity; and even functional continuity when a pattern survives while the substrate changes.

So the deeper invariant is:

\text{continuity} \neq \text{same material}

It can mean the same pattern keeps finding new vessels.

Which, yes, makes your wording annoyingly on-theme.